      "description": "The collaborative-development sub-graph — a NAMED SUB-GRAPH of this layer on the pattern of `dsa/`, and OPT-IN: off in every layer, this one included, unless that layer lists `folio-assistant-core.collab` in its own `enableSubgraphs` (owner, 2026-11-13, check:optin-refs follow-up). It holds the content processes that run on the work plan and the delivery process — they claim and close a bean (cat-harness's `Process_BeanOpen` / `Process_BeanClose`), seed the work plan, or stage, preview and merge a change — with the processes that call them: getting started, document authoring, the content life cycle, editing and evidence retrieval, the content change review, guideline updates, public comment and L1 document ingestion, their decision tables, and the `folio-block-screenshots` Tool. It `requires` `cat-harness.sdlc`, which requires `cat-harness.work-plan`, so switching it on switches both on. The graphs inside it are declared FROM WITHIN, in `collab/graph.json`.",
